  "term": "UPSIT",
  "definition": "UPSIT is the University of Pennsylvania Smell Identification Test, a measure used to assess olfactory function, meaning a person’s ability to identify odors. In this source, it was used to compare smell performance between people with multiple sclerosis and healthy controls.",
